Subject: [PATCH 6/9] =?UTF-8?q?firestore:=20give=20shared=5Fdecks=20a=20ru?=
 =?UTF-8?q?le=20=E2=80=94=20it=20never=20had=20one?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

js/app-features.js writes shared_decks/{id} at :1065 and reads it back at
:1119 for the ?sharedDeck= short links. The collection is absent from
firestore.rules, so both calls hit the default deny. Either deck sharing has
been quietly broken since it shipped, or live was hand-edited in the Console
and this file drifted — the exact failure the file header records for
2026-06-12. Writing the rule down makes the answer observable either way.

- read: open. The link is the capability and the recipient is usually signed
  out; the payload is a public decklist. (ids are 6 chars from a 55-char
  alphabet via Math.random() — unguessable enough for decklists, not secrets.)
- create: open, to match sharing working without an account like the rest of
  the deck builder, but bounded — exact key set, deck must be a map of at most
  120 entries, id at most 24 chars — so it can't serve as free storage.
- update/delete: denied. A handed-out link must not change under the recipient.

Deliberately no byte cap: .size() on a map counts keys, not bytes, so such a
clause would read like a limit and enforce nothing. Firestore's 1 MiB document
limit is the real backstop.

FIRESTORE_RULES.md carries an embedded copy of this file; snippet and table
updated to match, per the header's instruction.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ld5WCR1Wjb95tBgocvSXbH
---
 FIRESTORE_RULES.md | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 firestore.rules    | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 50 insertions(+)

diff --git a/FIRESTORE_RULES.md b/FIRESTORE_RULES.md
index 7e565371..d11250a2 100644
--- a/FIRESTORE_RULES.md
+++ b/FIRESTORE_RULES.md
@@ -31,6 +31,21 @@ service cloud.firestore {
       allow read, write: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == uid;
     }
 
+    // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+    // Shared decks — the ?sharedDeck=<id> short links. Had no rule at all
+    // until 2026-08-17, so both the write and the read hit the default deny.
+    // read is open because the link IS the capability; create is bounded so
+    // an open endpoint can't be used as free storage; update/delete denied.
+    // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+    match /shared_decks/{shareId} {
+      allow read: if true;
+      allow create: if shareId.size() <= 24
+        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['deck', 'order', 'archetype', 'source', 'timestamp'])
+        && request.resource.data.deck is map
+        && request.resource.data.deck.size() <= 120;
+      allow update, delete: if false;
+    }
+
     // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     // Public profile index — used by Testing Groups to add members
     // by email. Each user writes their own entry; anyone signed in
@@ -151,6 +166,7 @@ Changes propagate within a minute.
 |---|---|---|
 | `users/{uid}/**` | Owner only | Owner only |
 | `publicProfiles/{uid}` | Any signed-in user | Owner only |
+| `shared_decks/{shareId}` | Anyone with the link | Create only, bounded; no update/delete |
 | `testingGroups/{id}` | Members only | Owner (full) / Editor (data only) / Viewer (none) |
 | `testingGroups/{id}/activity/{id}` | Members only | Append-only by any member |
 
diff --git a/firestore.rules b/firestore.rules
index 6feb16db..0380e0fe 100644
--- a/firestore.rules
+++ b/firestore.rules
@@ -32,6 +32,40 @@ service cloud.firestore {
       allow read, write: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == uid;
     }
 
+    // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+    // Shared decks — the ?sharedDeck=<id> short links produced by
+    // js/app-features.js:1065 (.set()) and read back at :1119 (.get()).
+    //
+    // This collection had NO rule at all, so both calls hit the default deny.
+    // Either deck sharing has been quietly broken since it shipped, or live
+    // was hand-edited in the Console and this file drifted again — the exact
+    // failure the header above records for 2026-06-12. Writing the rule down
+    // makes the answer observable either way.
+    //
+    // read is open on purpose: the link IS the capability, and the recipient
+    // is usually not signed in — that is what a share link is for. The payload
+    // is a public decklist, no user data. Note the id is only 6 chars from a
+    // 55-char alphabet (~1e10) and drawn with Math.random(), so treat these as
+    // unguessable-enough-for-decklists, not as secrets.
+    //
+    // create is open to match: sharing works without an account today, same as
+    // the rest of the deck builder. It is bounded instead — one write, capped
+    // size, required shape — so an open endpoint can't be used as free storage.
+    // update and delete are denied outright: a link, once handed out, must not
+    // change under the recipient.
+    match /shared_decks/{shareId} {
+      allow read: if true;
+      allow create: if shareId.size() <= 24
+        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['deck', 'order', 'archetype', 'source', 'timestamp'])
+        && request.resource.data.deck is map
+        && request.resource.data.deck.size() <= 120;
+        // No byte cap here: .size() on a map counts keys, not bytes, so a
+        // "< 200000" clause would read like a size limit and enforce nothing.
+        // The 120-entry deck cap is the real bound (a legal deck is 60 cards);
+        // Firestore's own 1 MiB document limit backs it up.
+      allow update, delete: if false;
+    }
+
     // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     // Public profile index — used by Testing Groups to add members
     // by email. Each user writes their own entry; anyone signed in
